  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-7-PPR-4000006323</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-7" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Netherlands</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Encouraging transformative leadership of women to support food and nutritional security in two municipalities of Camag&#xfc;ey - CAPROCA.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This proposal aims to empower women leading family farms in Gu&#xe1;imaro and Jimaguay&#xfa; (Camag&#xfc;ey province) and to increase their resilience in the face of the impacts of climate change. The project seeks to promote gender equality and to encourage female leadership to reduce gender gaps that persist in the agricultural sector. This proposal is part of an integral project (CAPROCA) which has contributions from the French Development Agency and the French NGOs Socorro Popular Franc&#xe9;s and CCFD Terre Solidarity. Dutch contribution will complement the activities planned within the framework of CAPROCA, in particular those related to awareness, training, visibility and support in access to resources and opportunities, to achieve greater participation of women in farms, cooperatives and organizations of the agricultural sector. The implementation period would be framed between November 2022 and January 2024.</narrative>
  </description>
